※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4581

※ Writing through a reference that does not allow it is refused wherever it is
※ written, and a releasing write is a write.  The ordering says what other
※ observers see and changes nothing about who may write.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: mut u32 = 5u32
    let r: &u32 = &v
    ⎕release(r, 9u32)
    0u6
